/**
 * Metadata for every public, indexable route — the single source of truth for
 * three consumers that used to drift apart:
 *
 *   1. <SEO> tags rendered at runtime (what Google sees after it runs the JS)
 *   2. public/sitemap.xml            (generated by scripts/prerender.mjs)
 *   3. the prerendered static HTML   (what link-preview crawlers see, since
 *                                     they never run the JS at all)
 *
 * Plain ES module with no JSX or React imports on purpose: scripts/prerender.mjs
 * imports it directly under Node at build time.
 *
 * Adding a public page means adding it here. Login-gated routes must NOT be
 * listed — they render <SEO noindex> instead.
 */

